      "playwright": "Time was the hard part and the clock API made it tractable: install at a fixed instant, pauseAt a few seconds later, then fastForward whole minutes so assertions can use exact mm:ss strings instead of ranges. fastForward was preferred over runFor because the page ticks every 250 ms and replaying every frame for a 30-minute span is slow. Randomness is pinned with ?seed= and a mulberry32 PRNG, so the charter text is asserted verbatim. The prefix shortcut (typing 'q: ') was exercised with pressSequentially rather than fill, since it reacts to individual input events — which is how the first run caught a stray leading space.",
