      "playwright": "Most of this page follows standard ARIA patterns, so role-based locators (getByRole('tab'), getByRole('region', { name })) serve as the assertion and the accessibility check at once. The discount math is recomputed in the test rather than hard-coded, so a price change can't hide a formula bug. Swipes are sent with locator.dispatchEvent('pointerdown'/'pointerup') and clientX coordinates, which works the same on the desktop and Pixel 7 touch profiles without depending on the touchscreen API. The hero mock is the one timing-sensitive part: page.clock.install then pauseAt, then runFor in one-second steps until the run reports done, which is robust to small changes in spec durations. Reduced motion is checked with emulateMedia.",
